# Build context for the backend image. The Dockerfile is built from the
# repository root and only needs the manifests, the backend sources and the
# lockfile. Excluding the installed dependency trees keeps the context small
# and stops host-specific node_modules (including platform-native binaries
# built for the developer's OS) from leaking into the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.test.example
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.vscode
**/.idea
docs
**/audit-out.json
**/*-out.txt
